 "summary": "Assume ν > 0 and that (u, p, f, K) satisfies the bundled CandidateProperties: smooth periodic fields on the pre-singular domain, zero initial velocity, divergence-free, solving Navier–Stokes with force f on 0<t<1, and speed unbounded at t=1. Under these assumptions the Lean theorem proves four energy conclusions: ‖f(t)‖_{L²} is interval-integrable on [0,1]; the dissipation is integrable on [0,1); for every T∈[0,1), ‖u(T)‖² + 2ν∫₀ᵀ D ≤ (∫₀ᵀ‖f‖)²; and the analogous total bound 2ν∫_{[0,1)} D ≤ (∫₀¹‖f‖)² holds. The excerpt only says Lemma 10.4 gives 'global energy and integrated dissipation bounds for the localized fields directly from their equation'. That is consistent with this declaration, but the exact statement is not in the excerpt. The main caveat is that l2Norm, l2Sq, dissipation, the domain helpers and SpeedUnboundedAtOne are not shown, so the normalisations and integration domain cannot be checked.",
 "glossary": [
