  {"theorem": "candidate_energy_estimates", "line": 53, "plain": "For ν>0 and any u, f, p, K satisfying CandidateProperties ν u p f K, the following four conclusions hold: (i) t ↦ ‖f(t)‖_{L²} is interval-integrable on [0,1]; (ii) t ↦ dissipation u t is Lebesgue-integrable on [0,1); (iii) for every T∈[0,1), ‖u(T)‖²_{L²} + 2ν∫₀ᵀ dissipation u ≤ (∫₀ᵀ‖f‖_{L²})²; (iv) 2ν∫_{[0,1)} dissipation u ≤ (∫₀¹‖f‖_{L²})²."}
